# --- Local/submission mode (default) ---
# No values needed here at all: the app runs standalone with a local SQLite file
# (created automatically by `npm run dev`) and the dry-run call provider.

# --- Netlify deployed mode ---
# Set these when deploying to Netlify so the app uses a hosted Turso (libSQL) database
# instead of an on-disk file, which would not survive across serverless invocations.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://<your-db>.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Real calls (opt-in, off by default) ---
# Only set DRY_RUN=false + CALLE_API_KEY (+ ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) when you deliberately want to
# place a real CALL-E phone call. Leave unset to stay in dry-run everywhere.
#
# CALL-E has no separate "API key" page — it's an OAuth-protected MCP server. A dashboard-style
# API key (https://dashboard.heycall-e.com/account/api-keys, format iams_live_...) is for a
# DIFFERENT CALL-E surface and will NOT work here — the MCP endpoint this app talks to
# (.../mcp/openagent_oauth) only accepts the CLI's OAuth token. Get that value by:
#   1. npm install -g @call-e/cli
#   2. calle auth login          (opens a browser to authorize)
#   3. Read the cached token's `token.access_token` field from the printed cache path,
#      e.g. ~/.calle-mcp/cli/<hash>/token.json — that string is CALLE_API_KEY.
# The token is long-lived (about 1000 days), so this is a one-time setup step.
# DRY_RUN=false
# CALLE_API_KEY=
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (real calls only): CALL-E's real API never returns the qualification
# answers as structured data (see lib/call/calle.ts) — only as prose in the call summary/
# transcript. lib/call/extract.ts makes one cheap Claude Haiku call after a real call completes
# to turn that prose back into the flat answer shape dispatch.ts scores. Not needed in dry-run
# (fake.ts fabricates structured answers directly) or if you only ever run DRY_RUN=true.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
